---
title: Socket-Based Container Networking Topology (2026-04-15)
description: ovsbr0 privacy fabric + NAT route to ens3 uplink. No veth, loopback-only containers.
---

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph 'Host WG Clients wg0'
        WG[wg0 Clients 10.0.0.x]
    end

    subgraph 'ovsbr0 Privacy Fabric (10.88.88.1/24)'
        OVS[ovsbr0 Bridge<br/>fail-mode: standalone<br/>OpenFlow TCP:6653]
        WGCF[wgcf WARP<br/>172.16.0.2]
        GRPC[grpc-bridge<br/>control plane]
        SOCK[ovsbr0-sock anchor<br/>internal no IP<br/>unix socket dispatch]
        PRIVXRAY[priv_xray egress]
    end

    subgraph 'services Container (Incus)'
        LOOP[lan0-service = lo<br/>127.0.0.1/8<br/>nextdns UDP/TCP:53]
        UNIX[/run/services0/dns.sock]
    end

    subgraph 'Host NAT + Uplink'
        NAT[iptables NAT<br/>127.0.0.0/8 → ens3]
        ENS3[ens3 uplink<br/>148.113.204.83/32]
        INTERNET[internet]
    end

    subgraph 'OpenFlow table=0 (pri 200)'
        DNSIN[match udp tp_dst=53<br/>actions: output ovsbr0-sock]
        DNSOUT[match in_port=ovsbr0-sock udp tp_src=53<br/>actions: output priv_xray]
        SEC[Security Lv1<br/>drop invTCP/frag/ct<br/>TTL=64]
    end

    WG --> SOCK
    WGCF --> OVS
    GRPC --> OVS
    SOCK --> OVS
    PRIVXRAY --> OVS
    OVS --> DNSIN --> SOCK
    SOCK --> DNSOUT --> PRIVXRAY
    OVS --> SEC

    LOOP -->|bind 127.0.0.1:53| UNIX
    UNIX -.->|dispatch| SOCK
    LOOP -.->|outbound NAT| NAT
    NAT --> ENS3 --> INTERNET

